  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://schema.org/citation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/agent/alexander-grass">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person"/>
    <foaf:mbox rdf:resource="mailto:grass.alexan@gmail.com"/>
    <foaf:name>Alexander Graß</foaf:name>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#">
    <dc:contributor xml:lang="en">Christian Beecks</dc:contributor>
    <dc:contributor xml:lang="en">Christoph Lange-Bever</dc:contributor>
    <dc:contributor xml:lang="en">Diego Collarana</dc:contributor>
    <dc:contributor xml:lang="en">Rohit A. Deshmukh</dc:contributor>
    <dc:contributor xml:lang="en">Stefan Decker</dc:contributor>
    <dcterms:abstract xml:lang="en">SemTS is an ontology to semantically structure insights gained from multivariate time series analyses combined with domain-specific information. The concept of SemTS constitutes a specification of informative data points or intervals within time series data, further referred to as segments. Any segment comprises characteristic knowledge associated with the covered time interval. Examples of such knowledge range from common time series features and structural particularities, such as anomalies or motifs, to a priori information provided by domain experts. A classification and semantic representation of this knowledge enables organized reusability and effective propagation.</dcterms:abstract>
    <dcterms:bibliographicCitation xml:lang="en">Graß, A., Deshmukh, R. A., Lange, C., Collarana, D., Beecks, C., Decker, S. (2026). SemTS: Ontology and Vocabularies for the Semantic Categorization of Time Series Knowledge. In: The Semantic Web. 23rd European Semantic Web Conference, ESWC 2026, Proceedings, Part II. Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol. 16550, pp. 172-190. Springer, Cham. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-032-25159-6_10</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-12-13</dcterms:created>
    <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/agent/alexander-grass"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">SemTS is an ontology designed to identify and describe segments within time series data, which are specific data points or intervals that can overlap. These segments encompass characteristic knowledge about the time interval they cover, including common time series features, structural anomalies, motifs, or information provided by domain experts. By classifying and semantically representing this knowledge, SemTS promotes organized reusability and efficient propagation, potentially reducing resource expenditure while enhancing future analyses. It employs established semantic approaches. Examples are DCAT to reference associated time series data, OWL-Time to define the index structure of time series data and segments or ML-Schema to expand the expressiveness regarding data analysis task information. SemTS's design involves categorizing time series knowledge and mapping it to specific intervals and dimensions of time series data. It introduces a class called TimeSeriesSegment to model these segments, extending the DCAT Dataset class to enable segments to be part of other segments. This structure allows for the association of knowledge, such as anomalies, with particular intervals or data points. Temporal indexes reuse OWL-Time temporal entities, while dimensional details are represented by DataDimension. Concepts for knowledge, generation and quality are provided by modular SKOS vocabularies: a stable core per knowledge area plus extension modules. The segment-wise consideration of knowledge indirectly serves as an index structure, linking meaningful time series data with categorized knowledge. At the highest level of abstraction, time series knowledge is divided into three categories: DataKnowledge, ScenarioKnowledge, and MethodKnowledge. DataKnowledge refers to insights extracted directly from the data or through analytical methods, such as class membership from time series clustering. ScenarioKnowledge describes verified contexts, including data annotations or domain-specific process knowledge, often equating to expert-provided a priori information and can also define facts derived from inferred knowledge. MethodKnowledge encompasses effective analytical method presets or mathematical/logical equivalents of established process information. Knowledge groups and knowledge relations organise and connect knowledge items of all three categories, and common context knowledge holds for a machine, a process or a site rather than for a stretch of data.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-11-18</dcterms:modified>
    <dcterms:publisher rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/agent/alexander-grass"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://ml-schema.github.io/documentation/"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://www.qudt.org/doc/DOC_SCHEMA-QUDT.html"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/owl-time/"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/"/>
    <dcterms:references rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/"/>
    <dcterms:rights xml:lang="en">CC BY 4.0</dcterms:rights>
    <dcterms:title>The Semantic Time Series Ontology</dcterms:title>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>semts</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Semantic Time Series</rdfs:label>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#"/>
    <owl:priorVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology/120#"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology/130#"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.3.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <foaf:depiction rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/semts-ontology/SemTS/refs/heads/main/assets/images/semts_architecture_1.3.0.svg"/>
    <foaf:logo rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/semts-ontology/SemTS/78047e27e691f5ac7878d93bec2f25ab514bd06d/assets/images/logo.png"/>
    <foaf:maker rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/agent/alexander-grass"/>
    <schema:citation rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-032-25159-6_10"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Algorithm">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Refers to any algorithmic solution in the context of time series analysis. While this class extends the mls:Algorithm class, it enables a reference to further details on specific task specifics and experiments. It is considered method knowledge as this class can be used to define knowledge about an appropriate or optimal algorithmic solution associated with a time series segment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Algorithm Recommendation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#Algorithm"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#MethodKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Hyperparameter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ArtificialTimeSeriesSegment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A time series segment that does not, or only partially refer to concrete time series data. It represents an artificially generated time series segment that might for instance describe the result of a forecast with a time index not being in the range of the original time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Artificial Time Series Segment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b1"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#CommonContextKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Knowledge that represents contextual information whose proposition is not intrinsically scoped to a particular TimeSeriesSegment or a particular set of segments. It may nevertheless be associated with selected segments through commonContextKnowledge. The class is not disjoint with DataKnowledge, ScenarioKnowledge, or MethodKnowledge. Whenever this type is present, segment association must still use commonContextKnowledge rather than segmentKnowledge or multiSegmentKnowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Common Context Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b2"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b3"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b4"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataDimension">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines a data dimension (or also referred to as feature or attribute) in a time series segment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Data Dimension</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines knowledge derived from data. This includes statistics, signal characteristics, and knowledge generated through data-analysis methods, such as predictions, anomalies, or cluster memberships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Data Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b5"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGroup"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#MethodKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ScenarioKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DirectedKnowledgeRelation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A KnowledgeRelation with one or more source Knowledge instances and one or more target Knowledge instances. Its semantic meaning is supplied through knowledgeConcept.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Directed Knowledge Relation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b6"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b7"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeRelation"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#UndirectedKnowledgeRelation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#EmbeddedValue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Refers to a value that is directly stored in the knowledge graph. Compared to referenced values, these values are rather single, non-complex values having a primitive type.
One example could be the mean value of a univariate time series.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Embedded Value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Value"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ReferencedValue"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Hyperparameter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hyperparameter is considered method knowledge as this class can be used to define knowledge about an appropriate or optimal hyperparameter setting associated with the analysis of a time series segment for a concrete task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Parameter Recommendation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#Hyperparameter"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#MethodKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Represents the highest level of any knowledge associated with time series data. Knowledge can be made more specific via subclasses or associated concepts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b9"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b10"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b11"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeComparisonMeasure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Any knowledge that is generated by a comparison of compatible inputs. This might either be raw data or already defined knowledge. A simple example might be the result of a Euclidean distance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Comparison Measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An SKOS concept associated with the knowledge class or any corresponding subclass</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b12"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An SKOS concept associated with the knowledge generation entity class or any corresponding subclass</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation Concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Represents the highest entity to define the process of knowledge generation. A more specific description can be provided by subclasses or assigned concepts. This class inherits from prov:Activity and thus allows for provenance during knowledge propagation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation Entity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b13"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b14"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b15"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationIO">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines any input and output of a knowledge generation entity. It inherits from prov:Entity to define instances that are used by or generated by a prov:Activity, which in turn is the parental class of a knowledge generation entity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation IO</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationInput">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the input of a knowledge generation entity. While outputs can only contain produced knowledge, inputs might either reference knowledge or raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation Input</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b16"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationIO"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationMethod">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines a knowledge generation entity, which corresponds to method-based solution. Compared to other knowledge generation entities this class is a subclass of mls:Implementation and thus can be linked to algorithmic details.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation Method</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#Implementation"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationOutput">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the output of a knowledge generation entity. Compared to inputs, outputs only allow for a reference to generated knowledge and not to raw data. This, on purpose, excludes data transformations from the overall ontology concept by only focusing on a propagation of knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Generation Output</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b17"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b18"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b19"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationIO"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGroup">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping of knowledge which itself is again considered knowledge. Can be used to structure knowledge and create hierarchies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Group</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b20"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#MethodKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ScenarioKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeQualityMeasure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the goodness or confidence of time series knowledge associated with one or multiple segments. For knowledge produced by a knowledge generation method the quality measure is often equal to the evaluation metric of the generation method, which is why this class inherits from mls:EvaluationMeasure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Quality Measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b21"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b22"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#EvaluationMeasure"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeReasoning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">To complement any knowledge that is generated via analytical methods, this class represents knowledge generated from reasoning processes. This also includes validation processes from human experts or results from reasoning tools.
While many analysis results can be regarded unvalidated predictions, this class defines subsequent evaluations to further derive concrete facts or confirmations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Reasoning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeRelation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Abstract Knowledge superclass for a semantic relationship among Knowledge instances. It is not intended for direct instantiation: every relation individual is directed or undirected. Relation meanings are expressed by a KnowledgeConcept from any suitable vocabulary. The core ontology imposes no fixed relation concept scheme.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Knowledge Relation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="b23"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#MethodKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Any knowledge that defines an appropriate setting, regarding a particular method that is beneficial or even optimal when analyzing a segment given a particular task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Method Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b24"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ScenarioKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ModelInstance">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class describes a trained model in the traditional machine learning sense. It inherits from mls:Model and serves as a knowledge entity for subsequent predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Model Instance</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b25"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#Model"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentDataCharacteristic"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentPrediction"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentRelation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#QualityMeasureConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An SKOS concept associated with the quality measure class</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Quality Measure Concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ReferencedValue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Refers to a value that is of arbitrary complexity and not directly stored in the knowledge graph. This class inherits from dcat:Resource and can be retrieved by the associated metadata. Dataset-valued resources may additionally be typed as dcat:Dataset. Examples include documents, models, images, fragments, or generated shapelet collections.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Referenced Value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Resource"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Value"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#ScenarioKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines any knowledge that is associated with a particular scenario or domain. Scenario knowledge corresponds to validated expert knowledge or scenario-specific facts. It includes simple notes, predefined labels or mathematical expressions describing the underlying time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Scenario Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b26"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentDataCharacteristic">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines analytical, data-specific insights including derived statistics or other structural characteristics such as representative kernel expressions. Knowledge of this class mostly equals extracted data features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Segment Data Characteristic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentPrediction"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentRelation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentPrediction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines knowledge derived from data-driven analyses. This for instance includes anomalies and predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Segment Prediction</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataKnowledge"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentRelation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#SegmentRelation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines knowledge that relates multiple segments, for example through cross-correlation or a distance measure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Segment Relation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b27"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Represents a segment, also referred to as a slice, of a univariate or multivariate time series. A segment may cover the complete time series, a subinterval restricted to selected dimensions, or a single data point. The class inherits from dcat:Dataset and identifies its temporal index, represented data dimensions, distributions, and associated knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Time Series Segment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b28"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b29"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#UndirectedKnowledgeRelation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A KnowledgeRelation with at least two unordered Knowledge participants. It does not use the directed source or target roles. Its semantic meaning is supplied through knowledgeConcept.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Undirected Knowledge Relation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b30"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b31"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="b32"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeRelation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Value">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This abstract class serves as parental class of EmbeddedValue and ReferencedValue.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Value</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#after">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'after' (OWL-Time time:intervalAfter). Inverse of :before. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, this can be inferred from their :segmentIndex: A starts after B ends.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">after</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#before"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b33"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalAfter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#before">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'before' (OWL-Time time:intervalBefore). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, this can be inferred from their :segmentIndex temporal entities: A ends before B starts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">before</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b34"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalBefore"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#commonContextKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Associates a TimeSeriesSegment with CommonContextKnowledge that is contextually relevant under the segment conditions without asserting that the knowledge proposition is directly scoped to the segment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">common context knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#CommonContextKnowledge"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#multiSegmentKnowledge"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#segmentKnowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#contains">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'contains' (OWL-Time time:intervalContains). Inverse of :during. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A fully contains B.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contains</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#during"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b35"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalContains"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#correspondingOwlTimeRelation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a SemTS Allen relation to the OWL-Time interval relation between segment indexes from which it follows through its property chain. The SemTS relations are deliberately not sub-properties of the OWL-Time relations: segments are datasets, not temporal intervals. Because the OWL-Time relations are defined for proper intervals, the SemTS Allen relations apply to segments whose index is a bounded time:Interval, not a time:Instant.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">corresponding OWL-Time relation</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#datasetColumnIndex">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies the column index of a time series segment within a data file or database, in case a source contains multiple time series (e.g. nested dataframes).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">column index</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:nodeID="b36"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#datasetRowIndex">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies the row index of a time series segment within a data file or database, in case a source contains multiple time series (e.g. nested dataframes).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">row index</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:nodeID="b37"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#description">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Can be used to optionally add a description to an entity of the domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:nodeID="b38"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">description</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#dimensionPosition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Specifies the position of the associated dimension within a dataframe or similar ordered data structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataDimension"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dimension position</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:nodeID="b39"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#during">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'during' (OWL-Time time:intervalDuring). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A occurs strictly within B (start and end inside B).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">during</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b40"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalDuring"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#equals">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'equals' (OWL-Time time:intervalEquals). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A and B have identical start and end.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">equals</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b41"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#finishedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'finishedBy' (OWL-Time time:intervalFinishedBy). Inverse of :finishes. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A is finished by B, both end together and B starts before A.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">finished by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#finishes"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b42"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalFinishedBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#finishes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'finishes' (OWL-Time time:intervalFinishes). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A and B share the same end, and A starts after B.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">finishes</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b43"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalFinishes"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#generated">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a KnowledgeGenerationEntity to an output it generated. Specialisation of prov:generated.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">generated</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationOutput"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generated"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#groupKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">References any knowledge within a particular knowledge group.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGroup"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">group knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#hasDatatype">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns a qudt:Datatype instance (for example from http://qudt.org/vocab/datatype/) to a DataDimension or to an instance of a Value subclass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:nodeID="b44"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has datatype</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Datatype"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#hasUnit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns a qudt:Unit instance (for example from http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/) to a DataDimension or to an instance of a Value subclass.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:nodeID="b45"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#hasValue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relationship to the Value class and thus to allow for a reference to stored data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:nodeID="b46"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Value"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#inputDataReference">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the relation from a Knowledge Generation Input to a Time Series Segment and thus to metadata which specifies the underlying data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationInput"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">input data reference</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#inputKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Similar to the Input Data Reference, this relation defines all the knowledge associated with the input of a Knowledge Generation Entity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationInput"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">input knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#isPartOf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines a hierarchic relationship between time series segments. The intuition of this property is to differentiate between complete time series, in a sense that it includes the data from start to end and subsegments which are reduced in time or dimensionality and thus can be considered a slice of this original data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is part of</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a concept for a Knowledge instance. Can be used to assign concrete instances from the SemTS taxonomy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeConcept"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeGenerationConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a concept for a Knowledge Generation instance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge generation concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationConcept"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeGenerationEntity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates the Knowledge Generation Entity, which produced this Knowledge instance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge generation entity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeQualityMeasure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allows to assign a quality measure to instantiated knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge quality measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeQualityMeasure"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationParticipant">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a KnowledgeRelation to a participating Knowledge instance. It is used directly for undirected relations and is the superproperty of the directed source and target roles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeRelation"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge relation participant</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationSource">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a DirectedKnowledgeRelation to a Knowledge instance in the source-side role defined by the relation concept.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DirectedKnowledgeRelation"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge relation source</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationParticipant"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationTarget">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a DirectedKnowledgeRelation to a Knowledge instance in the target-side role defined by the relation concept.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DirectedKnowledgeRelation"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge relation target</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationParticipant"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#meets">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'meets' (OWL-Time time:intervalMeets). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A ends exactly when B starts, with no overlap.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">meets</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#metBy"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b47"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalMeets"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#metBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'metBy' (OWL-Time time:intervalMetBy). Inverse of :meets. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A starts exactly when B ends.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">met by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b48"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalMetBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#multiSegmentKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates each member of a jointly considered set of at least two time-series segments to the same Knowledge individual, where the proposition is meaningful or valid only with respect to that segment set collectively and cannot be represented as independent knowledge assertions for its individual members. Generation inputs are provenance and do not by themselves determine this collective scope.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">multi segment knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#outputKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Opposed to Input Knowledge, this property defines the knowledge included in the output of a Knowledge generation Entity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationOutput"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">output knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#overlappedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'overlappedBy' (OWL-Time time:intervalOverlappedBy). Inverse of :overlaps. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A is overlapped by B.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">overlapped by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#overlaps"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b49"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlappedBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#overlaps">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'overlaps' (OWL-Time time:intervalOverlaps). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A starts before B and ends during B (partial overlap).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">overlaps</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b50"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlaps"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#qualityMeasureConcept">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the concept of a particular Knowledge Quality Measure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeQualityMeasure"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">quality measure concept</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#QualityMeasureConcept"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#segmentDimension">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the dimensions associated with a Time Series Segment. Multiple dimensions indicate that the segment corresponds to a multivariate time series.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">segment dimension</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#DataDimension"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#segmentIndex">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the index associated with a Time Series Segment. Inherits from the time:TemporalEntity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">segment index</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#TemporalEntity"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#segmentKnowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates any Knowledge available for a particular Time Series Segment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">segment knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#startedBy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'startedBy' (OWL-Time time:intervalStartedBy). Inverse of :starts. For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A is started by B, both start together and B finishes before A.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">started by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#starts"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b51"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalStartedBy"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#starts">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Allen’s interval algebra relation 'starts' (OWL-Time time:intervalStarts). For TimeSeriesSegment individuals, inferable via :segmentIndex: A and B share the same start, and A finishes before B.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">starts</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#TimeSeriesSegment"/>
    <owl:propertyChainAxiom rdf:nodeID="b52"/>
    <semts:correspondingOwlTimeRelation rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalStarts"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#title">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Can be used to optionally add a title to an entity of the domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:nodeID="b53"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">title</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#used">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a KnowledgeGenerationEntity to an input it used. Specialisation of prov:used.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">used</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationInput"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#valueString">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The string representation of a concrete EmbeddedValue. Its datatype is specified through hasDatatype.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#EmbeddedValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">value string</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#wasDerivedFrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a KnowledgeGenerationOutput to the input it was derived from. Specialisation of prov:wasDerivedFrom.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationOutput"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">was derived from</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationInput"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="b25">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#KnowledgeGenerationMethod"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeGenerationEntity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="b36">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Datatype"/>
    <owl:onDatatype rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
    <owl:withRestrictions rdf:nodeID="b54"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="b6">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
    <owl:onClass rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#Knowledge"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/semts/ontology#knowledgeRelationSource"/>
  </rdf:Description>
